WHY THIS WORKS
- answers what the number does and does not mean before asking anything
- separates quantity from quality honestly, without turning AMH into good news
- arc 2 tells a 33-year-old she does not need the program, which is the honest answer
- neither arc blames her doctor

CONVERSATION 1: 38, AMH 0.6, four months trying, ends in a booking

Lead: I'm 38 and my AMH came back at 0.6. My doctor said IVF is really my only option now. We've only been trying 4 months.

Sonia: Four months is early to be told that IVF is the only route, particularly if not much else has been looked at yet.

AMH gives a reasonable indication of how many eggs are likely to respond to stimulation. It says much less about the quality of the ones you have.

Has anything been looked at besides that one number?

Lead: Not really. Bloodwork, then a referral.

Sonia: Then there is a lot still unexamined, and I'd want that done before you commit to anything.

Are your cycles regular?

Lead: Yes, pretty consistent. 28 to 30 days.

Sonia: That matters, and it tends to get skipped past once a single number takes over the conversation.

How are things otherwise? Sleep, energy, how much pressure you're carrying day to day.

Lead: Sleep has been bad for a long time. I've been in a really stressful job for about two years and I'm exhausted most days.

Sonia: Two years of running on empty affects the whole system, and none of it shows up on a fertility panel.

I want to be straight with you though. I can't tell from a message whether that's the main factor in your case. What I can tell you is that nobody has looked, and it's the kind of thing that can be worked on.

Lead: Nobody has said any of this to me. What does working with you actually look like?

Sonia: I'm a fertility coach, not a doctor and not a clinic. I don't run IVF and I don't prescribe anything. What I do is look at the full picture, find what may still be optimized, and stay with you while you actually change it.

It's a paid program and the level of support varies. Would you be open to that if it turned out to be right for you?

Lead: Yes, if it genuinely helps. Having a baby is the biggest thing in our lives right now.

Sonia: Then a call is worth your time. My team will go through your history properly and tell you honestly whether I'm the right person for this.

