CONVERSATION 2: 33, not trying yet, ends with a free resource and no link

Lead: hi! saw your reel about AMH. mine came back 1.1 and I'm 33. we're not trying yet but it really freaked me out

Sonia: At 33, not trying yet, I wouldn't let that number frighten you.

It's a rough guide to how many eggs might respond to stimulation. It doesn't predict whether you'll conceive naturally, and it isn't a countdown.

Lead: ok that's a relief. should I be doing something about it now though?

Sonia: Probably nothing dramatic.

Is anything else worrying you? Irregular cycles, pain, anything a doctor has flagged.

Lead: no, everything else has been normal. I just want to be prepared when we do start.

Sonia: Then you're in a better position than most, and you don't need a program like mine yet.

The women I work with are usually already trying and running into something specific. If that changes, or something comes up, come back and I'll help you look at it properly.

Lead: that's really honest, thank you. anything worth doing in the meantime?

Sonia: Watch my masterclass when you've got a spare hour. It covers what actually matters in the year before you start trying, and you'll be ahead of most people.

